-- Are the indicators reported for the timestep that produced them, or summed
-- over the report interval?  Three of the four events here fall away from the
-- monthly report boundaries, so the rows they land on answer the question.
--
--   B-1H  a CECON CON limit closes two connections on days 7.1 and 19.1.
--   C-1H  an ACTIONX tightens WECON in April, and its limit bites on days 182
--         and 504.
--
-- Per timestep, each event appears on the ministep row that produced it, and
-- report boundaries without an event are zero.  Per report interval, the next
-- boundary would carry the event instead.  What matters is which row it lands
-- on, not the count.  Do not add RPTONLY or summary thinning to this deck: they
-- discard the ministep rows the comparison needs.  The day-182 event coincides
-- with a report boundary and therefore does not discriminate between the two.

INCLUDE
 'include/wpwe-model.inc' /

SUMMARY
INCLUDE
 'include/wpwe-summary.inc' /

SCHEDULE
TUNING
 2.0 3.0 1.0e-4 /
 /
 /

INCLUDE
 'include/wpwe-wells.inc' /

CECON
 'B-1H' 2* 3 4 0.6 2* 'CON' /
/

ACTIONX
 'LATECON' 1 /
 YEAR = 2020 AND /
 MNTH = APR  AND /
 DAY  >= 10      /
/
WECON
 'C-1H' 2* 0.6 2* 'CON' /
/
ENDACTIO

DATES
  01 'FEB' 2020 /
  01 'MAR' 2020 /
  01 'APR' 2020 /
  01 'MAY' 2020 /
  01 'JUN' 2020 /
  01 'JUL' 2020 /
  01 'AUG' 2020 /
  01 'SEP' 2020 /
  01 'OCT' 2020 /
  01 'NOV' 2020 /
  01 'DEC' 2020 /
  01 'JAN' 2021 /
  01 'FEB' 2021 /
  01 'MAR' 2021 /
  01 'APR' 2021 /
  01 'MAY' 2021 /
  01 'JUN' 2021 /
  01 'JUL' 2021 /
/
END
